description\": \"lowest wide light level (about 97 % of the footprint) that carries the stair arms and has the largest flat area\", \"count\": 1}], \"repeated_elements\": [{\"what\": \"round studs on the upward faces of the terraces\", \"pitch_relative_to_largest_extent\": 0.0547, \"count\": null}, {\"what\": \"equally spaced terrace levels\", \"pitch_relative_to_largest_extent\": null, \"count\": 8}]}, \"capture\": {\"likely_origin\": \"manual_modelling\", \"defects\": [\"thin diagonal lines on light surfaces suggest triangulated or merged brick faces\", \"435 connected components, so the model consists of many separate bricks\"], \"floor_or_background_included\": false}, \"evidence\": [{\"id\": \"E1\", \"statement\": \"Four views from the sides show a symmetrical stepped taper with about eight receding levels.\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"strong\"}, {\"id\": \"E2\", \"statement\": \"The top view shows a black cross: one axial black stair strip on each of the four sides, meeting in the centre.\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"strong\"}, {\"id\": \"E3\", \"statement\": \"The surfaces carry round studs in a regular grid, and the model has 435 separate components, consistent with plastic building bricks.\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"strong\"}, {\"id\": \"E4\", \"statement\": \"A small dark block with light openings sits at the summit, reading as a shrine or temple.\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"moderate\"}, {\"id\": \"E5\", \"statement\": \"Facts: footprint profile is a stepped taper (base ratio 0.966, top ratio 0.012), with 8 regularly spaced levels at a spacing of 0.09 of the height.\", \"source\": \"facts\", \"strength\": \"strong\"}, {\"id\": \"E6\", \"statement\": \"Facts: mirror symmetry about both horizontal axes is high, 4-fold rotation is medium, and mirror about up is low. The model is only roughly 4-fold symmetric.\", \"source\": \"facts\", \"strength\": \"moderate\"}, {\"id\": \"E7\", \"statement\": \"Colours are only near-black (59 %) and near-white (41 %), with grayscale-like appearance (mean saturation 0.03).\", \"source\": \"facts\", \"strength\": \"moderate\"}, {\"id\": \"E8\", \"statement\": \"The staircase on each side is a single central strip, narrow relative to the terrace width, and the summit block is small relative to the base (top ratio 0.012 for the topmost extent).\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"moderate\"}, {\"id\": \"E9\", \"statement\": \"Extents are 0.0959 x 0.0959 x 0.0715, so height is about 75 % of the base width, which gives a fairly low pyramid.\", \"source\": \"facts\", \"strength\": \"weak\"}, {\"id\": \"E10\", \"statement\": \"The black strips are one stud-row wide stacked bricks with a stepped profile, so the stairs are steep and brick-built rather than carved into every terrace.\", \"source\": \"views\", \"strength\": \"weak\"}], \"hypotheses\": [{\"id\": \"H1\", \"label\": \"Pyramid-like monument with four stairs and a summit temple (brick-built model of a stepped temple-pyramid)\", \"confidence\": 0.8, \"supports\": [\"E1\", \"E2\", \"E4\", \"E5\"], \"weakens\": [\"E9\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H6\"], \"specializes\": null, \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"stepped pyramid with temple\", \"kind\": \"type\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"step pyramid\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"Many abstract stepped designs share terraces and a top block without representing any real monument.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"stepped terraces\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E1\", \"E5\"]}, {\"feature\": \"axial stairs on all four sides\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E2\"]}, {\"feature\": \"temple or shrine on top\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E4\"]}, {\"feature\": \"square plan with 4-fold symmetry\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E6\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H2\", \"label\": \"Mesoamerican temple-pyramid (Maya or Aztec type) with a summit temple\", \"confidence\": 0.6, \"supports\": [\"E1\", \"E2\", \"E4\"], \"weakens\": [\"E8\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H4\"], \"specializes\": \"H1\", \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"Mesoamerican pyramid\", \"kind\": \"type\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"Mesoamerican pyramids\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"Four-sided axial staircases and a small summit shrine also occur in Egyptian-style, Khmer or pure fantasy pyramids.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"four axial staircases\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E2\"]}, {\"feature\": \"small temple on a flat summit\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E4\"]}, {\"feature\": \"nine terraces (as at El Castillo)\", \"observed\": \"partly\", \"evidence\": [\"E5\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H3\", \"label\": \"El Castillo (Temple of Kukulcan), Chichen Itza\", \"confidence\": 0.3, \"supports\": [\"E2\", \"E4\", \"E5\"], \"weakens\": [\"E8\", \"E9\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H5\"], \"specializes\": \"H2\", \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"El Castillo, Chichen Itza\", \"kind\": \"individual\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"El Castillo Chichen Itza\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"The real building has 9 terraces, 91 steps per stairway and a wider stair, and the model shows about 8 levels with narrow stair strips and no distinct balustrades.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"four stairways, one per side\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E2\"]}, {\"feature\": \"9 terraces\", \"observed\": \"partly\", \"evidence\": [\"E5\"]}, {\"feature\": \"single-chamber temple on top\", \"observed\": \"partly\", \"evidence\": [\"E4\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H4\", \"label\": \"Other Maya pyramids (e.g. Temple of the Inscriptions, Tikal temples) or Aztec Templo Mayor type\", \"confidence\": 0.1, \"supports\": [\"E1\", \"E4\"], \"weakens\": [\"E2\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H3\"], \"specializes\": \"H2\", \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"Maya temple-pyramid\", \"kind\": \"type\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"Maya pyramid\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"These usually have a single front staircase, while the model has four of them.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"one dominant staircase\", \"observed\": \"no\", \"evidence\": [\"E2\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H5\", \"label\": \"Top structure as temple or shrine chamber with openings\", \"confidence\": 0.5, \"supports\": [\"E4\"], \"weakens\": [\"E8\"], \"alternative_to\": [], \"specializes\": \"H1\", \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"pyramid temple\", \"kind\": \"type\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"pyramid temple\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"The summit block is small and could merely be a decorative cap or a finishing brick stack.\", \"about\": \"P3\", \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"roof-like cap\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E4\"]}, {\"feature\": \"openings or doorway\", \"observed\": \"partly\", \"evidence\": [\"E4\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H6\", \"label\": \"Free design without a real-world model (generic brick pyramid)\", \"confidence\": 0.3, \"supports\": [\"E6\", \"E7\"], \"weakens\": [\"E4\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H1\"], \"specializes\": null, \"candidate\": {\"label\": null, \"kind\": \"none\", \"wikidata_search_term\": null}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"The four-fold stairs and the summit shrine are specific features that make a deliberate reference to temple-pyramids likely.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"simple strict black/white scheme\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E7\"]}, {\"feature\": \"approximately symmetric build without irregular details\", \"observed\": \"yes\", \"evidence\": [\"E6\"]}]}, {\"id\": \"H7\", \"label\": \"Egyptian-style or other non-Mesoamerican step pyramid (e.g. Djoser, Khmer temple mountain)\", \"confidence\": 0.1, \"supports\": [\"E1\"], \"weakens\": [\"E2\", \"E4\"], \"alternative_to\": [\"H2\"], \"specializes\": \"H1\", \"candidate\": {\"label\": \"Pyramid of Djoser\", \"kind\": \"individual\", \"wikidata_search_term\": \"Pyramid of Djoser\"}, \"strongest_counterargument\": \"Djoser has six steps and no stairs or summit temple, whereas the model has four axial stairs and a top structure.\", \"about\": null, \"feature_checks\": [{\"feature\": \"four axial stairs\", \"observed\": \"no\", \"evidence\": [\"E2\"]}, {\"feature\": \"six terraces\", \"observed\": \"no\", \"evidence\": [\"E5\"]}]}], \"questions_for_owner\": [\"Is the model based on a real monument or a game or film setting, and which one?\", \"How many terraces and how many steps per stairway does the brick model have by design?\", \"What do the light bricks on the top block represent (windows, doorway, decoration)?\", \"Was the model built from physical bricks and scanned, or built digitally?\", \"Is the black-and-white colour scheme intentional (for example reflecting limestone and shadowed stairs) or caused by available bricks?\"], \"notes\": \"Hypotheses overlap and are not exclusive. The 435 components and stud grid favour a brick-built toy. Scale is an estimate based on a typical 8 mm stud pitch and may be wrong.\"}"^^rdf:JSON .

ex:lego3_object a crm:E18_Physical_Thing ;
    rdfs:label "Object shown by lego3"@en ;
    dct:description "Square stepped pyramid built from studded bricks: light grey/white terraces with four black central stair arms forming a cross in plan, topped by a small dark temple-like block with light openings."@en ;
    dct:format "brick_built_toy" ;
    dct:medium "plastic building bricks (studded, black and white/light grey)"@en ;
    dct:type "building_or_monument" ;
    crm:P43_has_dimension ex:lego3_levels,
        ex:lego3_size ;
    crm:P46_is_composed_of ex:lego3_P1,
        ex:lego3_P2,
        ex:lego3_P3,
        ex:lego3_P4 ;
    rdfs:comment "Overall shape: stepped taper (truncated pyramid) with square footprint, four axial stair arms, small superstructure on top. Mirror axes: a, b; rotational fold: 4."@en .

